    "the_epistemic_clock_indexing_proof": "Colleague 6 provided the definitive mathematical resolution to the 'clock tick' dispute: Round 1 (t=1) evaluates depth k=1 (direct visual counts); Round 2 (t=2) evaluates depth k=2 (actions conditioned on Round 1 broadcast, e.g. Seat 2 in T_L); Round 3 (t=3) evaluates depth k=3 (actions conditioned on Round 2 broadcast, e.g. Seat 5 refuting T_L via Seat 2's silence). Thus, depth k=3 executes precisely at Round 3 (t=3), NOT Round 4. Camp 4's claim that depth k executes at t=k+1 had an off-by-one indexing error that would have delayed Seat 2 in T_L to Round 3.",
